###############################################################################
# 0. DOCUMENT CONTROL
###############################################################################

DOC_ID          = PREHISTORIC_COMPLEXITY_CATALOG
TITLE           = Catalog of prehistoric cases that challenge a surplus-
                  first civilization model
AUDIENCE        = research, teaching, product, and data teams
IMPLEMENTATION  = treat this file as the source of truth for field names,
                  allowed values, and record structure

###############################################################################
# 1. PURPOSE AND SCOPE
###############################################################################

1.1 PURPOSE
  Define a maintainable catalog of well-documented prehistoric cases that
  complicate this traditional sequence:

    agriculture -> surplus -> hierarchy -> cities / monuments / specialized
    knowledge / "civilization" crystallizing around 3500 BCE in
    Mesopotamia and Egypt.

  In-scope challenges include:
    - monumental construction by hunter-gatherers
    - dense settlement without palaces or visible ruling class
    - specialized technical skill earlier than expected
    - long-duration oral geographic memory
    - graphic systems before Sumerian proto-writing
    - complex society with little reported warfare evidence
    - claimed Ice Age coastal cities (included only as contested claims)

1.2 OUT OF SCOPE
  This catalog does not assert a replacement global chronology.
  It does not treat mythic, literary, or fringe claims as demonstrated
  archaeology unless evidence_grade says otherwise.
  It does not encode excavation methods, lab protocols, or legal status.

1.3 NORMATIVE LANGUAGE
  MUST / MUST NOT / SHOULD / MAY are requirements on catalog records
  and implementations, not on ancient people.

###############################################################################
# 2. CONVENTIONS
###############################################################################

2.1 TIME
  Primary date fields MUST use calibrated calendar years BCE or CE.
  Optional date_cal_bp MAY be added as integer years before 1950 CE.
  Approximate ranges MUST use "~" only when the source range is itself
  approximate.
  Competing chronologies MUST be listed in chronology_notes, not hidden.
  Do not mix "years ago", "BP", and "BCE" in the same primary field.

  Conversion aid:
    cal BP approximately equals 1950 + BCE year
    example: 8000 BCE ~ 9950 cal BP

2.2 NAMES
  record_id MUST be lowercase ASCII snake_case.
  display_name SHOULD use the most common scholarly English form.
  local_or_alt_names MAY list other spellings.

2.3 GEOGRAPHY
  region MUST be a modern geographic descriptor, not a culture name.
  polity_today SHOULD name the present-day country or equivalent.

2.4 CLAIMS
  Each record MUST separate:
    established_facts   = widely accepted observations
    challenge_claim     = how the case pressures the traditional model
    caveats             = limits, debates, and non-equivalence warnings

  Absence of weapons, palaces, writing, or farming MUST NOT be written
  as proof of peace, equality, illiteracy, or pre-agricultural life
  unless independently supported.

###############################################################################
# 3. CONTROLLED VOCABULARIES
###############################################################################

3.1 record_type
  archaeological_site
  site_complex
  oral_tradition_corpus
  graphic_system
  contested_feature

3.2 subsistence
  hunter_gatherer
  hunter_fisher_gatherer
  herder
  early_farmer
  mixed
  unknown
  not_applicable

3.3 complexity_class
  monument
  dense_settlement
  earthwork
  technical_specialization
  graphic_notation
  long_memory
  contested_lost_city

3.4 evidence_grade
  A  excavated, published, broadly accepted core facts
  B  excavated or well documented, interpretation debated
  C  mixed, partial, or chronology revised
  D  contested attribution or natural-feature dispute
  E  claim only; not demonstrated

3.5 claim_status
  demonstrated
  interpretive
  revised_chronology
  not_demonstrated
  natural_origin_preferred

3.6 traditional_model_target
  surplus_before_monuments
  farming_before_large_labor
  hierarchy_before_dense_settlement
  old_world_priority
  writing_begins_in_sumer
  warfare_as_organizer
  short_oral_memory
  ice_age_no_cities

###############################################################################
# 4. RECORD SCHEMA
###############################################################################

A record MUST contain the fields below, in this order.
Unknown values MUST be "unknown" or "not_applicable", never blank.

REQUIRED FIELDS
  record_id
  record_type
  display_name
  region
  polity_today
  date_range_cal_bce
  subsistence
  complexity_class
  builders
  key_feature
  established_facts
  challenge_claim
  traditional_model_target
  evidence_grade
  claim_status
  caveats

OPTIONAL FIELDS
  local_or_alt_names
  date_cal_bp
  related_record_ids
  chronology_notes
  implementation_notes

###############################################################################
# 5. VALIDATION RULES
###############################################################################

V1  record_id MUST be unique.
V2  compound places MUST be separate records.
V3  oral traditions MUST use record_type = oral_tradition_corpus
    and subsistence = not_applicable.
V4  challenge_claim MUST not exceed what established_facts plus caveats
    can support.
V5  "earliest known X" MUST be scoped (region, class, or publication
    status) or moved to caveats.
V6  If a popular date and a revised date both exist, both MUST appear.
V7  Contested artificiality MUST set evidence_grade to D or E and
    claim_status to not_demonstrated or natural_origin_preferred.
V8  Implementations MUST treat this schema as additive: new fields MAY
    be appended; required fields MUST NOT be renamed.

