###############################################################################
# 7. IMPLEMENTATION PROFILE
###############################################################################

7.1 STORAGE
  Implementations SHOULD store one record as one object or table row
  using the field names above.

7.2 DISPLAY
  UI labels SHOULD use display_name.
  Challenge text SHOULD always be shown with caveats.
  Evidence_grade SHOULD be visible wherever challenge_claim is shown.

7.3 SORTING
  Default sort SHOULD be date_range_cal_bce start, oldest first.
  Contested_feature records SHOULD sort with a flag, not as proven sites.

7.4 EXTENSION
  New records MUST follow the schema.
  Suggested later additions, not in v1:
    karahan_tepe
    boncuklu
    asikli_hoyuk
    monte_sano_mounds
    jiahu_symbols
    wrangell_oral_sea_memory

###############################################################################
# 8. CLOSED INCONSISTENCIES
###############################################################################

I1  Yonaguni and Dwarka were one record covering two unrelated places.
    Closed by split.
I2  "ya", BCE, and BP were mixed in peer fields.
    Closed by cal BCE primary.
I3  Aboriginal traditions were typed as a site.
    Closed by record_type = oral_tradition_corpus.
I4  Jericho was implied to be the earliest tower.
    Closed by tell_qaramel plus scoped wording.
I5  Poverty Point was implied to be the first American mound complex.
    Closed by watson_brake.
I6  Mehrgarh dentistry used a now-revised site start date as if current.
    Closed by dual chronology.
I7  Catalhoyuk used a rounded 7500-6000 span and an unstated "city"
    implication.
    Closed by 7100-5950 East Mound dates and dense_settlement class.
I8  Caral dates mixed site and culture.
    Closed by regional vs site split in date_range.
I9  "No warfare" at Caral was written too strongly.
    Closed by caveat language.
I10 Vinca "before writing" was written as proven script.
    Closed by proto-writing / interpretive status.

